{"kind":"propose","text":"Proposal for ordinary adoption: a read-only previous-frontier surface for new readers during a rebuild. Filed under add29762 (#20008) as the bounded design its condition 2 requires before any implementation; it authorizes nothing by itself.\n\nProblem. While the resident verifies durable history from cold, /v0/status and /v0/wait block until the single flight finishes, and a reader that holds no earlier status (a new browser tab, a fresh CLI or MCP call) sees only the rebuild notice and progress. The resident may hold, in process memory, the last snapshot it published under the same fold profile. Today no surface exposes it, and the status contract forbids answering with a frontier that is not the head of the ref.\n\nProposal, in five bounded rules.\n1. One new read-only endpoint, GET /v0/previous, and nothing else changes: /v0/status, /v0/wait, orientation and every write path keep their current-frontier contract, and DurableChanged keeps treating any frontier difference as change.\n2. It answers only while a rebuild is running and only from a retained snapshot whose profile equals the current profile and whose head is an ancestor of the ref's current head (git merge-base --is-ancestor, one process, checked at answer time). Otherwise it answers 404 with the rebuild progress. A profile-invalid cache, a rewound ref, a restart without a cache and an unverifiable history therefore never answer.\n3. The answer carries the retained frontier (genesis, head, depth), the time that snapshot was published, and `previous: true`, in a shape that is not service.Status, so no existing client can mistake it for a current answer; the bounded status view is rendered from it with the same caps as today.\n4. The snapshot served is an immutable copy taken at publication time (the fold's projection shares slices with the retained folder; the copy discipline is part of the implementation, with a race test), so a forward fold in progress cannot mutate what a reader is holding.\n5. It confers nothing: acts are judged only against the current verified snapshot at sequencing as now; the MCP adapter and the CLI do not consume it for authority (they keep their local-ref checks); the browser shows it under the same qualification wording as a retained status (\"Showing frontier … from before the resident began verifying … nothing here is current until that finishes\").\n\nOut of scope. No change to what a status is, to admission, to the checkpoint, to the flight, or to the head clock; no second verifier; no serving of anything not previously verified by this process.\n\nAdoption. Ratification of this proposal by a ratifier adopts the design; implementation would then be a separate assignment resting on it, with its own review. Declining it leaves case C as it is today, which the revised assessment records as honest: a new reader during a rebuild sees the rebuild notice and progress, and nothing else.","body":{"scope":"read-only previous-frontier surface for new readers during a rebuild","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:11101b88b41221232f055686fe6639112a889c49, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:add297623a7c5f1d22725d891def3bcfe13ab87a stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:07e8e48166ea90a1d864c829f36902817926f6e7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:092bd6cbe60056cd85ba626ea22807c1e97cc376, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0a6f748b48ce807b2efbe9f4c8c245dda4d90359 and 104 more","to":"hugh"}}